    "created_at": "2025-04-30T04:44:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-30T04:44:38Z",
    "body": "I think that's correct too. In theory, web platform tests are meant to be run as if you've started the browser from scratch for every test. If you want to test a series of documents, you need to use iframes or popup windows.\r\n\r\nIn practice, most browser/test runner combos do not do this. (This leads to annoying changes like https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/0a5ef44bf2e1c9be8f50beee9936771d5adcd35b ; see also https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/33590.) But the closer we can get to that ideal, the better.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
